      "text": "your land shall be desolate, Lev. 26:33 (Jer. 7:34). none of them that trust in him shall be desolate, Ps. 34:22. Let their habitation be desolate, Ps. 69:25 (Acts 1:20). Your country is desolate, your cities are burned, Isa. 1:7. to cause to inherit the desolate heritages, Isa. 49:8 (1 Ne. 21:8). thy waste and thy desolate places … be too narrow, Isa. 49:19 (1 Ne. 21:19). more are the children of the desolate, Isa. 54:1 (Gal. 4:27; 3 Ne. 22:1). make the land of Egypt desolate, Ezek. 32:15. desolate land shall be tilled, Ezek. 36:34. making thee desolate because of thy sins, Micah 6:13.",
